  "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by isolating the $(x-8)^{8}$ term and then taking the $8$th root of each side.\n\nFirst, let's isolate the $(x-8)^{8}$ term on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-8)^{8} & =1280 \\\\ (x-8)^{8} & =256\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the $8$th root of each side and solve for $x.$ Since the exponent $(8)$ is even, we consider both the positive and negative solutions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-8)^{8} & =256 \\\\ \\sqrt[8]{(x-8)^{8}} & =\\pm \\sqrt[8]{256} \\\\ x-8 & =\\pm \\sqrt[8]{{2}^{8}} \\\\ x-8 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =8\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=6$ and $x=10.$",
